Package: malt
Version: @VERSION@
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: MALT contributors <kamal@aferiad.xyz>
Homepage: https://github.com/NacreousDawn596/MALT
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-numpy, python3-scipy, python3-matplotlib
Recommends: python3-pyqt6
Description: A MATLAB-compatible language runtime powered by CPython
 MALT is a standalone language implementation for a documented MATLAB subset.
 It parses, semantically analyzes, and compiles MATLAB-like source to Python
 in memory, then executes it on NumPy, SciPy, and Matplotlib.
 .
 It provides a CLI, an interactive REPL, a source-level debugger, a language
 server (LSP), structured diagnostics with source maps, and a Qt6 notebook GUI.
